       "\n",
       "Here are some carefully crafted name suggestions:\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 1. **PageToScreen AI**\n",
       "**Why it works:** This name instantly communicates the core value proposition — taking written content (the \"page\") and transforming it into video (the \"screen\"). It's simple, memorable, and self-explanatory. The word flow mirrors the user journey itself. Anyone who hears this name immediately understands what the product does.\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 2. **StoryReel**\n",
       "**Why it works:** \"Story\" captures the literary input side (books, novels, scripts), while \"Reel\" evokes cinema and video production. It's short, punchy, and highly brandable. It has a modern, creative feel that appeals to both writers and content creators. Great for social media handles and app store discoverability. Think: *\"I made this on StoryReel.\"*\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 3. **InkMotion**\n",
       "**Why it works:** \"Ink\" represents the written word — manuscripts, scripts, novels — while \"Motion\" signals animation and video. Together, they paint a vivid picture of words literally coming to life through movement. It sounds premium, creative, and artistic, which could attract authors, screenwriters, and storytellers who take their craft seriously.\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 4. **NarrativeForge**\n",
       "**Why it works:** \"Narrative\" speaks directly to storytelling across all formats (books, screenplays, prompts), and \"Forge\" implies powerful creation and transformation — like a blacksmith forging raw material into something refined. It communicates that this is a **serious production tool**, not just a toy. It positions the platform as a full pipeline/workshop for content creation.\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 5. **SceneSpring**\n",
       "**Why it works:** \"Scene\" ties directly to visual storytelling and video output, while \"Spring\" suggests something flowing naturally and effortlessly — like content *springing to life* from text. It also evokes freshness and new beginnings. The name feels approachable and optimistic, perfect for marketing to users who have **no editing skills** but want professional results.\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## 6. **PlotCast**\n",
       "**Why it works:** \"Plot\" represents the story/script input, and \"Cast\" has a brilliant double meaning — it refers to both *casting characters* (with AI-generated voices and visuals) and *broadcasting/publishing* content. It's concise, catchy, and rolls off the tongue. Easy to remember, easy to spell, and highly domain-friendly.\n",
       "\n",
       "---\n",
       "\n",
       "## Quick Comparison\n",
       "\n",
       "| Name | Vibe | Best For | Memorable? |\n",
       "|------|------|----------|------------|\n",
       "| **PageToScreen AI** | Clear & descriptive | SEO & instant clarity | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n",
       "| **StoryReel** | Modern & sleek | Broad consumer appeal | ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n",
